  "id": "COMPOUND:34435 - PROTEIN:1658",
  "verbalization": "Ent-Gloeosteretriol appears to interact with Mitogen-activated protein kinase 14 through multiple indirect pathways, as evidenced by its targets in different biological contexts. The first pathway links Ent-Gloeosteretriol to Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, which is targeted by K-252a, a known inhibitor of mitogen-activated protein kinase 14. The second pathway connects Ent-Gloeosteretriol to DMS-53, which is targeted by Gerontoisoflavone A, another compound that modulates mitogen-activated protein kinase 14. The third pathway directly links Ent-Gloeosteretriol to mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase kinase 3, which is targeted by a complex molecule that ultimately affects mitogen-activated protein kinase 14. These findings suggest that Ent-Gloeosteretriol may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately influence the activity of mitogen-activated protein kinase 14. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Ent-Gloeosteretriol and mitogen-activated protein kinase 14, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
